; Limit 06: an L0 function cannot be the process entry point.
; Blocks job 7. The OS calls the C symbol `main` as int main(int, char **).
; An L0 def named main is the L0 program's main: spec section 9 fixes its
; signature to one (list int) parameter, and section 10.2 compiles it to
; @l0_f_main. L0 has no way to choose a symbol name, so the runtime's entry
; point cannot be given the name the OS looks for, and naming it main collides
; with the program.
;
; The first def is a program; the second is l0rt.c's main.

(def main ((input (list int))) (list int)
  input)

(def main ((argc int) (argv int)) int
  0)
